{"results":[{"url":"https://www.jsonline.com/picture-gallery/news/local/wisconsin/2020/01/13/judge-finds-wisconsin-election-officials-contempt-over-voter-rolls/4457150002/","final_url":"https://www.jsonline.com/picture-gallery/news/local/wisconsin/2020/01/13/judge-finds-wisconsin-election-officials-contempt-over-voter-rolls/4457150002/","title":"Judge finds elections commission in contempt of court","description":"\"I can’t be any clearer than this,\" Judge Paul Malloy said. \"They need to follow my order.\"","language":"en","text":"WISCONSIN\n\n# Judge finds elections commission in contempt of court\n\nMilwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nJan. 13, 2020, 2:26 p.m. CT\n\nOzaukee County Circuit Judge Paul Malloy held state election officials in contempt of court for not following his order to remove thousands of people from the voters rolls.\n\nMichael Sears / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nJudge Paul Malloy listens to attorneys from both sides before making his finding at the Ozaukee County Courthouse in Port Washington.\n\nMichael Sears / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nProtesters who watch the proceedings quietly filed out,  disappointed with the judge's finding. Ozaukee County Circuit Judge Paul Malloy held state election officials in contempt of court for not following his order to remove thousands of people from the voters rolls.\n\nMichael Sears / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nmembers of Souls to the Polls and other groups with an interest, fill the courtroom to hear the judge issue his decision at the Ozaukee County Courthouse in Port Washington. Ozaukee County Circuit Judge Paul Malloy held state election officials in contempt of court for not following his order to remove thousands of people from the voters rolls.\n\nMichael Sears / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nAssistant Attorney General Karla Keckhaver.\n\nMichael Sears / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nAttorney Rick Esenberg from Wisconsin Institute for Law and Liberty after the court ajourned. Ozaukee County Circuit Judge Paul Malloy held state election officials in contempt of court for not following his order to remove thousands of people from the voters rolls.\n\nMichael Sears / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nOzaukee County Circuit Judge Paul Malloy held state election officials in contempt of court for not following his order to remove thousands of people from the voters rolls. Before the courtroom session Gregory Lewis, the leader of Souls to the Polls led a protest outside the courthouse and spoke to media gathered outside theeOzaukee County Courthouse in Port Washington. Protestors had tape over their mouths symbolizing their voices being silenced.\n\nMichael Sears / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nProtesters from Souls to the Polls demonstrate outside the Ozaukee County Courthouse in Port Washington before the proceeding. Tape over their mouth to symbolize their voices being silenced by taking voters off the rolls. Ozaukee County Circuit Judge Paul Malloy held state election officials in contempt of court for not following his order to remove thousands of people from the voters rolls.\n\nMichael Sears / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nRev. Greg Lewis, president of Souls to the Polls, leads a protest outside of the Ozaukee County courthouse Monday, Jan. 13, 2020, over the ordered removal of voters from the rolls.\n\nPatrick Marley / Milwaukee Journal Sentinel\n\nFeatured Weekly Ad","author":"Milwaukee Journal Sentinel","published_date":"2020-01-13T20:26:47Z","latency_ms":561.0155220001616,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}